course: dictionary
lesson: 4977
title: Reading a reaction
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words show how a character feels or reacts, not what a thing looks like. «You did WHAT?» she asked, incredulous. The word incredulous tells you how she felt: she could hardly believe what she had heard.
explain: Look for clues around the word. The capital letters and the question mark in «You did WHAT?» show shock, and incredulous names that shock. Ask yourself: how would a person look or sound if they felt this way?
explain: Alice is often incredulous at the strange rules of Wonderland. Here the word shows a reaction to strange things, so it is about not believing them. In an old book you might meet «hitherto incredulous», which means not believing until now.
fact: Incredulous means not able or not willing to believe something.
fact: An incredulous look or voice shows that you do not believe what you see or hear.
fact: Incredulous describes a reaction, so in a story it tells you how a character feels.
fact: «Hitherto incredulous» means until now not believing.
fact: Incredulous is an adjective: incredulous, more incredulous, most incredulous.
exercise: «You did WHAT?» she asked, incredulous. What does incredulous show? | She was very hungry | She was sleepy | She was happy to go home | *She could not believe what she heard
exercise: Alice is often incredulous at the strange rules of Wonderland. Which word is closest in meaning? | Hungry | *Doubtful, unable to believe | Tired | Cheerful
exercise: Which sentence shows an incredulous reaction? | He ate his lunch quickly | *He stared at the magician, unable to believe the card had vanished | She laughed at the joke | She shut the door quietly
test: Which word means not able to believe something? | Curious | Jealous | *Incredulous | Nervous
test: «Hitherto incredulous» means what? | Valued highly | *Until now not believing | Silliness | Being very sorry
exam: Ben read the score twice with his mouth open. Which word best describes his reaction? | Bored | Cheerful | Sleepy | *Incredulous
